Realist paintings aim to represent people, objects, environments, and everyday situations as accurately as possible. They emphasize lifelike proportions, realistic details, natural lighting, and recognizable visual characteristics. These artworks often portray ordinary subjects and scenes without significant exaggeration, idealization, or abstract interpretation.
